WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.445 --> 00:00:01.895
- Now I want to say the
level of disrespect,

00:00:01.895 --> 00:00:04.406
but I believe that HR
people need to believe

00:00:04.406 --> 00:00:06.703
in themselves more and
have a bigger impact.

00:00:06.703 --> 00:00:08.825
Look at this guy, whaaaat?

00:00:08.825 --> 00:00:09.975
Right there.

00:00:09.975 --> 00:00:11.020
That's the Eiffel Tower.

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:11.858
- He's not taking us.

00:00:11.858 --> 00:00:13.771
- France, not the best place to travel to

00:00:13.771 --> 00:00:16.938
when you are on a calorie restriction.

00:00:19.061 --> 00:00:20.000
What's up Believe Nation?

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.973
Happy weekend.

00:00:20.973 --> 00:00:25.713
I am on my way to Paris, and
I'm taking you guys with me.

00:00:25.713 --> 00:00:27.100
- Not us.

00:00:27.100 --> 00:00:28.284
He's not taking us.
- [Evan] Not Nina.

00:00:28.284 --> 00:00:29.117
Not Nina.

00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:29.950
- Not me.

00:00:29.950 --> 00:00:30.783
- Or the dog.

00:00:30.783 --> 00:00:32.034
- [Evan] Not Haden.
- [Nina] Or Haden.

00:00:32.034 --> 00:00:34.450
- But you guys get to come.

00:00:34.450 --> 00:00:37.033
(upbeat music)

00:00:47.605 --> 00:00:50.355
(cheerful music)

00:00:56.096 --> 00:00:57.245
So I'm going to be speaking at an event

00:00:57.245 --> 00:01:00.478
in Paris for a company called Talentsoft

00:01:00.478 --> 00:01:03.777
and talking about the role of digital and

00:01:03.777 --> 00:01:07.442
leadership for the human-resource
industry, which is great.

00:01:07.442 --> 00:01:10.209
It came as a result of somebody that I

00:01:10.209 --> 00:01:13.167
worked with at Sage, who left Sage

00:01:13.167 --> 00:01:15.846
and went off to go to Talentsoft.

00:01:15.846 --> 00:01:18.809
And this happens a lot in B2B businesses.

00:01:18.809 --> 00:01:20.702
If you're selling to business, you want

00:01:20.702 --> 00:01:22.212
to make sure you have a great relationship

00:01:22.212 --> 00:01:24.364
with everybody involved,
because it's so often

00:01:24.364 --> 00:01:27.437
that people will jump from
one company to another.

00:01:27.437 --> 00:01:28.503
And if you had a great relationship,

00:01:28.503 --> 00:01:29.846
they're going to bring you with 'em.

00:01:29.846 --> 00:01:31.294
So I'm excited to go.

00:01:31.294 --> 00:01:33.416
I haven't been to Paris for, I want

00:01:33.416 --> 00:01:34.899
to say, five or six years.

00:01:34.899 --> 00:01:36.273
Last time I went was with Nina.

00:01:36.273 --> 00:01:38.708
And so, I'm at the airport,
a little bit early.

00:01:38.708 --> 00:01:39.958
Going to check in.

00:01:40.866 --> 00:01:43.719
Fighting some allergies,
so hopefully those go away.

00:01:43.719 --> 00:01:45.107
And I'm ready to have a great time.

00:01:45.107 --> 00:01:47.169
(cheerful music)

00:01:47.169 --> 00:01:48.246
It's one of the benefits about flying

00:01:48.246 --> 00:01:51.401
business class, which I
do for my corporate stuff.

00:01:51.401 --> 00:01:55.342
You get to go to the airport
lounges before taking off.

00:01:55.342 --> 00:01:57.145
So I got to find mine, relax, do a little

00:01:57.145 --> 00:02:00.364
bit of work, say hi to
Nina, then hop my flight.

00:02:00.364 --> 00:02:03.114
(cheerful music)

00:02:17.461 --> 00:02:20.041
So if you noticed from my
food, eatin' pretty light.

00:02:20.041 --> 00:02:21.888
I'm on a special new diet that my

00:02:21.888 --> 00:02:24.122
personal trainer put me on.

00:02:24.122 --> 00:02:24.955
(sniffs)

00:02:24.955 --> 00:02:25.863
Ooh, allergies.

00:02:25.863 --> 00:02:28.677
And I have to track
calories on a daily basis.

00:02:28.677 --> 00:02:29.747
So a lot of the stuff in there, I have

00:02:29.747 --> 00:02:31.563
no idea what it was, so I'm going to go

00:02:31.563 --> 00:02:35.040
find myself a Booster Juice downstairs.

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:36.429
France, not the best place to travel

00:02:36.429 --> 00:02:38.806
to when you are on a calorie restriction.

00:02:38.806 --> 00:02:39.639
(laughs)

00:02:39.639 --> 00:02:42.732
We'll see how it goes, and I'll
try to guess as best I can.

00:02:42.732 --> 00:02:45.482
(cheerful music)

00:02:47.282 --> 00:02:49.699
Alright, got my Bananas Away.

00:02:51.478 --> 00:02:52.823
Oh.

00:02:52.823 --> 00:02:54.832
It's good stuff.

00:02:54.832 --> 00:02:57.085
370 calories gives me,
like, six-hundy-something

00:02:57.085 --> 00:02:58.502
left for the flight.

00:02:58.502 --> 00:02:59.555
Fingers crossed.

00:02:59.555 --> 00:03:01.821
I got a little bit of (mumbles)
time before I check in.

00:03:01.821 --> 00:03:04.286
So I'm going to do some social media.

00:03:04.286 --> 00:03:07.175
I love answering people's questions

00:03:07.175 --> 00:03:09.118
on my phone, I'm on Twitter, Instagram,

00:03:09.118 --> 00:03:12.070
Snapchat at airports, flying.

00:03:12.070 --> 00:03:13.946
It's a great way to kill time and

00:03:13.946 --> 00:03:17.153
add some value to the community.

00:03:17.153 --> 00:03:19.903
(cheerful music)

00:03:20.827 --> 00:03:22.814
I was, uh, forgot to check in.

00:03:22.814 --> 00:03:25.910
I was the last to check
in in business class,

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.749
so I get the middle seat, but this

00:03:27.749 --> 00:03:29.706
is going to be pretty comfortable.

00:03:29.706 --> 00:03:30.749
I got good news.

00:03:30.749 --> 00:03:34.332
The guys next to me
are traveling together.

00:03:35.897 --> 00:03:38.436
So I don't have to sit
in the middle anymore.

00:03:38.436 --> 00:03:41.103
(new age music)

00:03:49.872 --> 00:03:52.455
(upbeat music)

00:03:55.020 --> 00:03:56.357
Alright, landed in Paris.

00:03:56.357 --> 00:03:57.455
Ooh, these chairs are cool.

00:03:57.455 --> 00:03:59.319
Check this out.

00:03:59.319 --> 00:04:03.818
Those lie-down chairs in
the plane were awesome.

00:04:03.818 --> 00:04:05.435
Couldn't sleep, though.

00:04:05.435 --> 00:04:08.559
Mix of congestion and
the guy coughing nonstop.

00:04:08.559 --> 00:04:10.929
I feel bad for the cougher.

00:04:10.929 --> 00:04:12.813
Seven hours straight.

00:04:12.813 --> 00:04:14.125
Must be rough.

00:04:14.125 --> 00:04:16.590
Anyway, happy to be here in Paris.

00:04:16.590 --> 00:04:20.545
Going to go find my Uber driver, I guess.

00:04:20.545 --> 00:04:22.590
There's some driver picking me up.

00:04:22.590 --> 00:04:23.556
I'm going to get to the hotel and

00:04:23.556 --> 00:04:25.705
try to get a little bit of sleep.

00:04:25.705 --> 00:04:29.047
It is seven in the morning, Paris time,

00:04:29.047 --> 00:04:31.532
and I'm looking forward
to starting this day.

00:04:31.532 --> 00:04:34.115
(upbeat music)

00:04:38.327 --> 00:04:41.368
This crazy line is the exit.

00:04:41.368 --> 00:04:43.376
I guess Customs is not going to find

00:04:43.376 --> 00:04:45.678
(drowned out by background
noise) anytime soon.

00:04:45.678 --> 00:04:47.510
So I'm standing in that crazy line.

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:49.340
It gives me a chance to answer

00:04:49.340 --> 00:04:51.848
some messages on social media.

00:04:51.848 --> 00:04:53.005
Alright, finally got out.

00:04:53.005 --> 00:04:55.010
That took at least an hour.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:56.150
That was crazy.

00:04:56.150 --> 00:04:59.223
Just got a message that my driver is here,

00:04:59.223 --> 00:05:00.827
waiting for me, worried that I'm not

00:05:00.827 --> 00:05:04.251
showing up, so I got to go find him.

00:05:04.251 --> 00:05:07.781
Very excited to get to
the hotel and sleep.

00:05:07.781 --> 00:05:10.698
(fast-paced music)

00:05:38.825 --> 00:05:40.832
Alright, I'm all checked in.

00:05:40.832 --> 00:05:44.189
Number 6083, ready to go
up, check out my room.

00:05:44.189 --> 00:05:46.538
So people like Xavier, who set me up here,

00:05:46.538 --> 00:05:49.340
my client, my friend,
asked me how my flight was.

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:53.423
So on the one hand, the
flight wasn't that great,

00:05:54.410 --> 00:05:58.440
you know, no wi-fi,
the TV system went down

00:05:58.440 --> 00:06:01.008
and lost my spot in the movie.

00:06:01.008 --> 00:06:02.389
I couldn't sleep because of my allergies,

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:03.344
couldn't sleep because this guy was

00:06:03.344 --> 00:06:06.427
coughing ahead of me the whole night,

00:06:07.307 --> 00:06:09.449
so, you know, not the best experience.

00:06:09.449 --> 00:06:12.054
But on the other hand, the food was great,

00:06:12.054 --> 00:06:14.574
I got to sit on the aisle because that guy

00:06:14.574 --> 00:06:16.732
wanted to sit with his friend, you know,

00:06:16.732 --> 00:06:19.381
I got those awesome seats that reclined.

00:06:19.381 --> 00:06:22.470
And overall, it was a
good experience, and so

00:06:22.470 --> 00:06:25.487
was it a good flight, was it a bad flight?

00:06:25.487 --> 00:06:26.407
Well, it was both.

00:06:26.407 --> 00:06:27.341
It really just depends on what

00:06:27.341 --> 00:06:29.007
side of the coin you look at it.

00:06:29.007 --> 00:06:32.352
I think that applies to most
of the things in our lives.

00:06:32.352 --> 00:06:33.269
It's 10:30.

00:06:35.115 --> 00:06:36.698
I got here at 7:00.

00:06:37.657 --> 00:06:39.813
It's been three-and-a-half hours

00:06:39.813 --> 00:06:43.587
through security and
everything else to get here.

00:06:43.587 --> 00:06:45.920
And I'm grateful, I'm happy.

00:06:47.036 --> 00:06:48.869
I'm ready to sleep, but I'm happy

00:06:48.869 --> 00:06:50.502
to be in the hotel, I have a place to go.

00:06:50.502 --> 00:06:52.623
And so with every
situation, there's always

00:06:52.623 --> 00:06:53.848
something you can find that's negative,

00:06:53.848 --> 00:06:56.253
and there's always something
you can find that's positive.

00:06:56.253 --> 00:06:58.528
Is it a good flight or a bad flight?

00:06:58.528 --> 00:07:01.854
Is that thing you're facing
right now good or bad, too?

00:07:01.854 --> 00:07:03.392
It just depends on your outlook.

00:07:03.392 --> 00:07:05.021
Try to look on the positive side.

00:07:05.021 --> 00:07:06.349
Think it may help.

00:07:06.349 --> 00:07:08.823
Think I'm here, 6082.

00:07:08.823 --> 00:07:10.490
Look at these doors.

00:07:12.499 --> 00:07:13.499
Ahahahahaha.

00:07:14.793 --> 00:07:15.626
Alright.

00:07:16.879 --> 00:07:18.572
Look at this.

00:07:18.572 --> 00:07:19.655
Bathroom with

00:07:21.156 --> 00:07:24.408
That's pretty funky to have in the shower.

00:07:24.408 --> 00:07:25.383
Got a nice bathroom.

00:07:25.383 --> 00:07:27.286
Look at that guy, whaaaat?

00:07:27.286 --> 00:07:29.034
Let's go in.

00:07:29.034 --> 00:07:30.753
Oh, I've got two little beds.

00:07:30.753 --> 00:07:32.428
That's cool.

00:07:32.428 --> 00:07:34.012
Maybe I can squish 'em together.

00:07:34.012 --> 00:07:36.090
Got my TV, get some CNN on.

00:07:36.090 --> 00:07:37.653
Look at those lamps.

00:07:37.653 --> 00:07:38.700
That's pretty cool.

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:39.817
Oh, these are those showers that are,

00:07:39.817 --> 00:07:42.747
it's kind of a little bit see-through.

00:07:42.747 --> 00:07:44.961
You can't actually see through,
but the light gets through.

00:07:44.961 --> 00:07:46.038
Look at this view.

00:07:46.038 --> 00:07:49.066
Paris, (speaking French)

00:07:49.066 --> 00:07:49.899
How is it?

00:07:49.899 --> 00:07:52.132
(speaking French)

00:07:52.132 --> 00:07:55.756
Oh, man, my French, my
French has to come back.

00:07:55.756 --> 00:07:57.162
Alright, so we're going to set up,

00:07:57.162 --> 00:07:59.230
have a quick nap, see how much

00:07:59.230 --> 00:08:02.257
time I have left afterwards, and

00:08:02.257 --> 00:08:04.846
practice my speak, go see Xavier.

00:08:04.846 --> 00:08:06.474
If I have a little bit of time,

00:08:06.474 --> 00:08:08.455
go check out some of the scenes

00:08:08.455 --> 00:08:11.455
around here, take you guys with me.

00:08:11.455 --> 00:08:14.038
(gentle music)

00:08:25.466 --> 00:08:29.045
Alright, so, got about
five hours' nap there.

00:08:29.045 --> 00:08:29.918
Wanted to sleep more, but I had to

00:08:29.918 --> 00:08:32.459
get up, because if I had a huge sleep,

00:08:32.459 --> 00:08:34.148
then I wouldn't sleep tonight,

00:08:34.148 --> 00:08:35.967
and tomorrow is an important day.

00:08:35.967 --> 00:08:37.501
Presentation day.

00:08:37.501 --> 00:08:40.280
So I've got a couple hours before

00:08:40.280 --> 00:08:43.197
meeting Xavier and going to dinner,

00:08:44.567 --> 00:08:45.539
which is interesting, because it's, like,

00:08:45.539 --> 00:08:47.386
10 o'clock in the morning for me.

00:08:47.386 --> 00:08:49.310
So I'm going to head onto the town,

00:08:49.310 --> 00:08:51.648
practice what I'm going to be thinking

00:08:51.648 --> 00:08:53.595
about for my speech, take in some

00:08:53.595 --> 00:08:55.687
of the sights, and have some fun.

00:08:55.687 --> 00:08:59.270
(leisurely Parisian music)

00:09:01.067 --> 00:09:03.619
So, figuring out the French
subway system has been fun.

00:09:03.619 --> 00:09:05.257
(laughs)

00:09:05.257 --> 00:09:07.055
Did a couple of wrong turns, but

00:09:07.055 --> 00:09:09.756
I think I finally know where I'm going.

00:09:09.756 --> 00:09:12.800
And I'm heading to the Champs-Elysees,

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:15.829
the most famous street in France,

00:09:15.829 --> 00:09:18.633
and I'm going to check
out the, what's it called?

00:09:18.633 --> 00:09:20.064
Arc de Triomphe.

00:09:20.064 --> 00:09:21.731
The Arch of Triumph.

00:09:22.819 --> 00:09:26.402
(leisurely Parisian music)

00:09:44.976 --> 00:09:47.413
So just behind me, oh, this side,

00:09:47.413 --> 00:09:49.926
right there, that's the Eiffel Tower.

00:09:49.926 --> 00:09:52.475
And seeing it, seeing back
there makes me miss Nina.

00:09:52.475 --> 00:09:56.163
Last time we came here, it
was, uh, it was a big surprise.

00:09:56.163 --> 00:09:58.496
We are off to Paris, France.

00:10:00.282 --> 00:10:01.199
- No. What?

00:10:02.730 --> 00:10:05.568
- [Evan] And we're on the
way to the airport right now.

00:10:05.568 --> 00:10:06.684
- Are you serious?

00:10:06.684 --> 00:10:08.048
- [Evan] Yeah.

00:10:08.048 --> 00:10:09.293
- Oh, my God, are you serious?

00:10:09.293 --> 00:10:10.126
(Evan laughs)

00:10:10.126 --> 00:10:10.959
No way.

00:10:12.317 --> 00:10:13.609
- I just showed up at her work.

00:10:13.609 --> 00:10:15.418
I booked an extra day off of her work,

00:10:15.418 --> 00:10:17.054
and we went for the weekend and came.

00:10:17.054 --> 00:10:19.279
It was Nina's first time to Paris.

00:10:19.279 --> 00:10:21.526
And I'm missing her right now.

00:10:21.526 --> 00:10:22.604
I hope she's doing okay.

00:10:22.604 --> 00:10:23.707
I got to bring her back now.

00:10:23.707 --> 00:10:24.826
It's a sign, I got to bring her back.

00:10:24.826 --> 00:10:26.595
Nina, I got to bring you back here.

00:10:26.595 --> 00:10:27.962
Got to bring you back here.

00:10:27.962 --> 00:10:28.795
Love you.

00:10:28.795 --> 00:10:32.378
(leisurely Parisian music)

00:10:46.502 --> 00:10:48.399
So they've really beefed up security

00:10:48.399 --> 00:10:49.975
since I came here last time.

00:10:49.975 --> 00:10:53.255
You can't even get in around the tower

00:10:53.255 --> 00:10:56.370
without security getting to the gates.

00:10:56.370 --> 00:10:58.379
It never used to be gated off like this.

00:10:58.379 --> 00:11:00.105
You had to pay to kind of go up

00:11:00.105 --> 00:11:03.229
to the various levels of the Eiffel Tower,

00:11:03.229 --> 00:11:05.042
but now you can't even get inside

00:11:05.042 --> 00:11:07.090
or close to it without
going through security.

00:11:07.090 --> 00:11:10.393
(drowned out by background noise)

00:11:10.393 --> 00:11:13.073
things you're not allowed to bring in.

00:11:13.073 --> 00:11:14.815
It's a little sad.

00:11:14.815 --> 00:11:16.396
It's a little sad that
it's kind of come to that.

00:11:16.396 --> 00:11:20.238
Hopefully it's a temporary
thing, but, uh, yeah.

00:11:20.238 --> 00:11:21.089
So I'm not going to go in.

00:11:21.089 --> 00:11:22.102
I don't have time to stand in line.

00:11:22.102 --> 00:11:24.060
I got to get back, got to have a shower,

00:11:24.060 --> 00:11:25.517
and then meet up with Xavier.

00:11:25.517 --> 00:11:28.545
I remember when I came here with Nina.

00:11:28.545 --> 00:11:30.131
I'm still at the Eiffel Tower.

00:11:30.131 --> 00:11:31.244
There it is.

00:11:31.244 --> 00:11:34.524
There were these flowers here,

00:11:34.524 --> 00:11:36.490
and Nina wanted to stop and look

00:11:36.490 --> 00:11:39.240
at them and just appreciate them.

00:11:40.358 --> 00:11:42.845
And that's what Nina loves doing.

00:11:42.845 --> 00:11:47.376
She loves appreciating nature
and appreciating the flowers.

00:11:47.376 --> 00:11:50.315
One of these bushes, I think
it's this bush, actually.

00:11:50.315 --> 00:11:51.982
You know, when I travel for business,

00:11:51.982 --> 00:11:53.647
I don't really do a lot
of the touristy things.

00:11:53.647 --> 00:11:54.548
I don't really need to.

00:11:54.548 --> 00:11:58.117
I'm not like, "Oh, my God,
it's the Eiffel Tower!"

00:11:58.117 --> 00:11:59.365
But I've been here a number of times

00:11:59.365 --> 00:12:01.279
already, too, so it's probably it.

00:12:01.279 --> 00:12:05.703
I'm a mix, so far, when
I'm doing this stuff, of

00:12:05.703 --> 00:12:08.827
one, just focusing on my
talk, what I'm going to say.

00:12:08.827 --> 00:12:11.387
You know, I'm missing four days for this,

00:12:11.387 --> 00:12:14.229
so I better deliver some
serious value tomorrow

00:12:14.229 --> 00:12:16.508
at my speech or I wasted my time here.

00:12:16.508 --> 00:12:19.306
And I always put that pressure on myself.

00:12:19.306 --> 00:12:20.611
So I got one side there.

00:12:20.611 --> 00:12:22.753
But the other side, I
just, I'm missing Nina

00:12:22.753 --> 00:12:24.041
A lot.

00:12:24.041 --> 00:12:26.090
I mean, I knew I'd miss her, but I'm

00:12:26.090 --> 00:12:27.941
missing her a lot more than I expected.

00:12:27.941 --> 00:12:29.076
I guess because of the history that we

00:12:29.076 --> 00:12:31.800
have here in this city and how I brought

00:12:31.800 --> 00:12:33.612
her here and the fun times we had.

00:12:33.612 --> 00:12:35.221
Don't want to travel without Nina.

00:12:35.221 --> 00:12:36.468
I'm missing her a lot.

00:12:36.468 --> 00:12:37.626
Anyway.

00:12:37.626 --> 00:12:40.009
Going to hop in the subway,
head back to the hotel,

00:12:40.009 --> 00:12:41.508
and have a quick shower, meet up

00:12:41.508 --> 00:12:43.163
with Xavier, and go for dinner.

00:12:43.163 --> 00:12:46.496
(fast-paced club music)

00:12:50.316 --> 00:12:52.037
It's a McDonald's over there.

00:12:52.037 --> 00:12:53.899
One of the things that
I always used to do.

00:12:53.899 --> 00:12:57.939
I wouldn't really care about
food in cities until Nina.

00:12:57.939 --> 00:12:59.527
I still don't really care that much.

00:12:59.527 --> 00:13:02.177
Just every time I travel,
now I need to book

00:13:02.177 --> 00:13:04.179
food in, because Nina loves
trying the local stuff.

00:13:04.179 --> 00:13:07.491
I would much rather just go in, just

00:13:07.491 --> 00:13:10.062
chill the city, see as
much stuff as possible,

00:13:10.062 --> 00:13:12.292
and stopping into a restaurant

00:13:12.292 --> 00:13:13.969
seemed to be, like, a waste of time.

00:13:13.969 --> 00:13:15.247
(laughs)

00:13:15.247 --> 00:13:18.272
I'm still not a huge fan,
but I would do it for Nina.

00:13:18.272 --> 00:13:19.105
But anyway, McDonald's used to

00:13:19.105 --> 00:13:20.939
always be my home when I traveled.

00:13:20.939 --> 00:13:24.597
Just in, out, try something
kind of, "kind of" local.

00:13:24.597 --> 00:13:25.505
I was always curious to see what

00:13:25.505 --> 00:13:26.560
they had that was different.

00:13:26.560 --> 00:13:28.318
McDonald's and Starbucks.

00:13:28.318 --> 00:13:30.615
So they had a blue-cheese bacon burger.

00:13:30.615 --> 00:13:31.722
I hate blue cheese.

00:13:31.722 --> 00:13:33.421
But even just thinking, it's what

00:13:33.421 --> 00:13:35.975
I always used to do, go to McDonald's

00:13:35.975 --> 00:13:37.724
and check out what's new and different

00:13:37.724 --> 00:13:41.261
and try that and take off, but, uh.

00:13:41.261 --> 00:13:42.644
I made it back.

00:13:42.644 --> 00:13:44.811
I've got 10 minutes to go.

00:13:45.843 --> 00:13:47.053
And I'm excited.

00:13:47.053 --> 00:13:49.636
(gentle music)

00:13:52.822 --> 00:13:55.155
Alright, had a great shower.

00:13:56.349 --> 00:13:57.842
Relaxed a little bit.

00:13:57.842 --> 00:13:59.971
Thought about what I was going to

00:13:59.971 --> 00:14:02.650
say tomorrow, refine my
speech, change my shirt.

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:03.483
Totally different shirt.

00:14:03.483 --> 00:14:05.071
Look at that amazing shirt.

00:14:05.071 --> 00:14:07.976
And now I'm going to
meet Xavier in the lobby.

00:14:07.976 --> 00:14:10.559
(gentle music)

00:14:12.174 --> 00:14:14.438
There he is, Mr. Xavier.

00:14:14.438 --> 00:14:15.355
How you doin'?

00:14:15.355 --> 00:14:16.465
- Hi, (mumbles).

00:14:16.465 --> 00:14:18.367
- (laughs) Boom.

00:14:18.367 --> 00:14:19.941
How you doin', man?

00:14:19.941 --> 00:14:20.899
(gentle music)

00:14:20.899 --> 00:14:22.298
I'm here on the Champs-Elysees

00:14:22.298 --> 00:14:24.214
with the founders of Talentsoft.

00:14:24.214 --> 00:14:25.381
There's one.

00:14:25.381 --> 00:14:26.749
Got more in the back, behind.

00:14:26.749 --> 00:14:30.798
Going to go have some
dinner, have some good talk.

00:14:30.798 --> 00:14:32.198
So excited.

00:14:32.198 --> 00:14:35.281
(calm, upbeat music)

00:14:37.345 --> 00:14:38.825
Now I want to say the level of disrespect,

00:14:38.825 --> 00:14:41.319
but I believe that HR
people need to believe

00:14:41.319 --> 00:14:43.609
in themselves more and
have a bigger impact.

00:14:43.609 --> 00:14:47.776
I'm frustrated that more CEOs
don't come from HR positions.

00:14:48.780 --> 00:14:51.413
You know, especially
North America (mumbles)

00:14:51.413 --> 00:14:53.677
doesn't come from HR, and I believe that

00:14:53.677 --> 00:14:56.169
we shouldn't just be complaining about it,

00:14:56.169 --> 00:14:58.942
we should be the leaders
and be the change.

00:14:58.942 --> 00:15:01.191
And tomorrow I'm going to go over some

00:15:01.191 --> 00:15:03.875
new ideas that I have that may
help you guys on your path.

00:15:03.875 --> 00:15:04.787
(audience laughs)

00:15:04.787 --> 00:15:06.317
And it's an honor to be here, and I've

00:15:06.317 --> 00:15:07.696
had some great discussions, and I see

00:15:07.696 --> 00:15:09.866
a lot of talent, a lot of
leadership in this room,

00:15:09.866 --> 00:15:11.722
and I hope that you'll
take the information

00:15:11.722 --> 00:15:13.274
that you learn tomorrow back home

00:15:13.274 --> 00:15:14.926
to your companies, and
I'm really just hoping

00:15:14.926 --> 00:15:17.619
to make a mark on your industry.

00:15:17.619 --> 00:15:18.452
- Thank you, Evan.

00:15:18.452 --> 00:15:19.479
- [Woman] Thank you very much.
(audience applauds)

00:15:19.479 --> 00:15:21.528
- Great group, great dinner.

00:15:21.528 --> 00:15:24.148
Some really awesome
conversations, actually.

00:15:24.148 --> 00:15:27.200
I taught people the handshake, pushed

00:15:27.200 --> 00:15:30.211
people to do bigger, bolder things,

00:15:30.211 --> 00:15:33.471
you know, usual Believe kind of stuff.

00:15:33.471 --> 00:15:34.664
It's, I don't know what time it is.

00:15:34.664 --> 00:15:36.404
I want to say 11 o'clock, Paris time.

00:15:36.404 --> 00:15:37.764
Ooh, I also got some macaroons.

00:15:37.764 --> 00:15:38.847
Look at this.

00:15:41.241 --> 00:15:43.080
Some yummy French macaroons.

00:15:43.080 --> 00:15:47.840
I probably destroyed my
calorie intake for the day.

00:15:47.840 --> 00:15:49.246
I'm going to head back to the hotel,

00:15:49.246 --> 00:15:51.959
probably practice my speech one more time,

00:15:51.959 --> 00:15:55.673
go through based on the new
information I kind of got today.

00:15:55.673 --> 00:15:57.059
I love really tailoring the content

00:15:57.059 --> 00:15:58.879
that I'm putting out, depending on

00:15:58.879 --> 00:16:00.804
the people, depending on the audience.

00:16:00.804 --> 00:16:02.178
So it's always great to be able to

00:16:02.178 --> 00:16:03.409
connect with the audience a little bit

00:16:03.409 --> 00:16:06.253
in advance, to just feel them out,

00:16:06.253 --> 00:16:08.490
hear what their challenges
are, and you can

00:16:08.490 --> 00:16:10.698
create something much better than just the

00:16:10.698 --> 00:16:14.745
standard thing that you
might deliver at an event.

00:16:14.745 --> 00:16:15.624
So that was good.

00:16:15.624 --> 00:16:16.974
So I'm going to rejig it a little bit,

00:16:16.974 --> 00:16:20.148
practice, see if I can get a hold of Nina,

00:16:20.148 --> 00:16:23.559
what she's up to, head to bed, wake up

00:16:23.559 --> 00:16:26.892
tomorrow morning, and let's go crush it.

